//? Title: VoxNet:genuine surface occupancy and explicit tensor MomentumSGD
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Classifying a3Dobject requires relating geometry to its category. Genuine original CAD surfaces become declared tensor occupancy grids;the complete original-width VoxNet shows every regularized MomentumSGD update and every held-out prediction.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/voxnet.cpp`.

> The method

Binary occupancy is mapped to[-1,1]before two3Dconvolutions,pooling and a128unit dense layer. The objective explicitly adds a weight-only sum-of-squares penalty:

$$ L=\frac1B\sum_i-\log\operatorname{softmax}(z_i)_{y_i}+\lambda\sum_{W}\|W\|_F^2,\qquad\nabla_W L=\nabla_W CE+2\lambda W. $$
\alttext(Mean categorical negative log likelihood plus lambda times the sum of squared weights;weight gradients add two lambda W,biases do not.)

The visible MomentumSGD loop fits all eight learned tensors. Four quarter-turn logits are averaged at inference. Reindexing this finite rotation orbit preserves the average up to floating-point accumulation order;this is discrete C4invariance,not arbitrary3Drotation invariance.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/voxnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/voxnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/voxnet_concept.tikz > build/voxnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/voxnet_concept.svg build/voxnet_concept.dvi > build/voxnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
